@page "/Pending"
@attribute [Authorize]
@layout BlankLayout

@* The last step of the Signup flow, not an error screen.

   Public self-registration is approval-gated, so an account arrives here the
   moment it is created: signed in, carrying no role, and unable to do anything
   until an administrator assigns one. RoleService.GetDefaultLandingRoute sends
   every role-less account here.

   It used to fall through to MainLayout and render inside the signed-in app's
   navigation chrome — a bar full of destinations the account cannot open —
   under the wording "אין לך אישור להשתמש במערכת!" and a placeholder support
   address. BlankLayout + AuthShell is what Login, Signup and Forget Password
   use, and this screen directly follows Signup.

   Nothing here reads the cascaded user. It could greet them by name, but this
   is reached by a forceLoad redirect and the cascaded User arrives a beat
   later, so the name would pop in after the page had already been read. *@

<AuthShell Title="החשבון נוצר בהצלחה"
           Subtitle="החשבון שלך ממתין לאישור.">

    <div class="lp-note" role="status">
        <svg class="lp-note-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="M12 7v5l3 2" />
        </svg>
        <span>לאחר אישור החשבון על ידי מנהל המערכת, ניתן יהיה להתחבר ולהתחיל לעבוד במערכת.</span>
    </div>

    @* The one action, and deliberately not a link to Home or the dashboard:
       this account cannot open either, so offering them is what would send a
       pending user around a loop of screens that refuse them. *@
    <a href="@PageRoutes.Login" class="lp-btn lp-btn-link">חזרה להתחברות</a>

</AuthShell>
